Goal: Finalize and validate the existing uncommitted work in this repository: fixes for DOG-035 and DOG-036 (see both entries in dogfood/findings/FINDINGS.md, the change_log.md entries, and documentation/ORCHESTRATE.md "Verification command").

DOG-035: `orchestrate --verify` used argparse nargs="+", so a verification command with its own flags failed with "unrecognized arguments". The change normalizes a single quoted CLI value with POSIX shell splitting (keeping an existing executable path whole), keeps Factory queue argv literal, reports malformed quoting as INVALID_VERIFICATION_COMMAND, and adds a quoting hint. DOG-036: the verification command's 300 s limit was fixed and undocumented; the change adds `--verify-timeout SECONDS` (1 to 3600) on new sessions and resume.

If the existing change is correct and complete, report IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS: NO_CHANGE_REQUIRED with reasons; otherwise fix only what is wrong and add tests. HowlPlane itself runs this repository's full regression gate (`make test-full`) after implementation and supplies the result to review and acceptance, so do not re-run the full suite yourself; targeted tests are enough. Reviewers: try to falsify both fixes, including every path that consumes --verify and --verify-timeout (new session, resume, Factory queue), interaction with the existing VERIFY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS default, documentation claims the code does not keep, and whether the tests would fail without the fixes.
